A, B, D, E, F and G are all versions of that single-source logic and remain within documented Edo manuscript practice:
* A = authorial self-censorship before presentation to the Shogun;
* B = moral/social scribal censorship of women’s martial knowledge, copied forward from a blank archetype;
* D = institutional Oniwaban redaction of state-secret techniques;
* E = aburidashi invisible-ink concealment that a non-initiated copyist would see as blank;
